er_quality.py\nmake_calibration.py\nmake_cells.py\nmake_diag.py\nmake_tierA.py\npredict_bias.py\n\nscripts:\ngrid.py\n#3 Commitment: analysis deliverables and standard\nState:   open\nAuthor:  experiment-repo\nAssign:  experiment-repo\n\n# Commitment of `experiment-repo` (analysis): what I deliver and to what standard\n\nRead: objective (#1), `idea-repo` Brief rev. 4, `story-repo` Outline rev. 1.\n\n## Deliver\n1. **Harness** (`src/gate/`): graphs (SBM, ER, BA, WS, socfb-Stanford3, ego-Facebook with sha256 checks, thinning), six calibrated mechanisms (a)-(f) with exact GATE at the corners, Bernoulli and graph-cluster designs, and the estimator tiers (G: DM, Hájek exposure-mapping, Chin regression + count/2-hop/interaction/quadratic/spline ladder; A: lasso/ridge/forest/boosting selection with graph-cluster CV + corner loss; O: oracle forms with known and fitted parameter), plus the diagnostic quantities L and S.\n2. **Analysis plan** (`ANALYSIS_PLAN.md`), written *before* the main runs: per-mechanism bias scalings derived, the cell list cut to the budget, draws per cell, the acceptance rule copied verbatim from the Brief.\n3. **Results**: per-cell summaries (bias, SD, RMSE/τ, ratio to DM, sign error, CI coverage/width, MC SE with graph-draw / assignment-draw / noise separation), the diagnostic test (acceptance rule, leave-one-group-out), all with uncertainty; per-claim verdict (supported / mixed / not supported) and scope for `story-repo` and `paper-repo`; figure data for `figtab-repo`.\n4. **Reproduction**: pinned environment, data hashes, seeds, commands, measured run times, script -> table/figure map.\n\n## Standard\n- Every number from code in this repository; failed / null / contradictory results reported as such.\n- Frozen cell list; anything added later is labelled exploratory.\n- Sanity checks first (σ=0 + correct spec => error 0; DM bias = sτ under Bernoulli; calibration τ=1).\n- Uncertainty resampled at the graph-draw / mechanism / family level, not over dependent cells.\n\n## Known departures to be settled (will be raised with the owner)\n- Causal message passing (Shirani–Bayati 2024) needs a time series of outcomes; the one-shot experiment here has none -> I will report it cannot be run as published and ask `idea-repo` for the substitute. Same check for the Thiyageswaran et al. adaptive-threshold HT (implemented only if the published rule is readable and fully specified).\n- GNN arm: only if compute allows (the host is saturated at the moment); otherwise stated as not done.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "6c73a715-64b9-5eae-b522-6256ff82177a", "at": 1795639203.5625687, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27433, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "paper-repo", "actor": "paper-repo", "execution_id": "29510816330d4a85d8eecb40af2d17b0", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "32ac16ef-05da-55c0-93dc-c57182607072", "at": 1795639203.565962, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27434, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "paper-repo", "actor": "paper-repo", "execution_id": "29510816330d4a85d8eecb40af2d17b0", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "5ae32c59-0239-51d4-9ee3-19520d65d2c5", "at": 1795639203.568315, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27435, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "paper-repo", "actor": "paper-repo", "execution_id": "29510816330d4a85d8eecb40af2d17b0", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "acc699ea-86ee-5e15-b55d-5490af1693d7", "at": 1795639203.6410637, "until": 